  "tagline": "A wire-compatible SQL cache for Postgres and MySQL that keeps cached queries fresh from replication.",
  "description": "Readyset sits between your application and Postgres or MySQL, speaking their wire protocols, and lets you cache specific SELECT queries. Instead of TTLs it consumes the database's replication stream and updates cached results incrementally using a dataflow engine derived from MIT's Noria research, so cached results stay within replication lag of the source. Uncached queries are proxied to the database. It suits read-heavy apps with repetitive queries that are tired of hand-built cache invalidation. Releases ship monthly under the Business Source License, with a managed Readyset Cloud option.",
